    "followUp": "What can make queryFn optional? A default query function configured with setQueryDefaults or setDefaultOptions can supply it when the query does not define one."
   },
   {
    "question": "What does queryFn receive?",
    "answer": "The function receives QueryFunctionContext rather than only the query key. This context lets the implementation use query metadata such as the key and request cancellation signal.",
    "followUp": "How should a fetch-based query function handle cancellation? Pass the context's signal to the request so cancellation can propagate to the underlying fetch."
